# Independent Tibetan-first proposals, C05:304–306

These are original Codex (GPT-6 Astra) proposals. All are PROVISIONAL and machine-matched; mechanical success is not semantic approval or hgm_gloss promotion.

The source origin is `ce646d0c48f9338ff47e40f46582ad14c8a3eaf4` through294. Source, context, original SQLite, external master/corpus and physical-source hashes were independently verified. The future through303 acceptance baseline is distinct and is not claimed here. Other angles and root judgments were not consulted. No source/repository files were changed, and work never required a W mutation hold.

Each segment folder contains `spec.json`, exact canonical `body.html`, `errata.json`, compact `report.md`, `intended-ranges.json`, `mechanical-proof.json`, and `errata-review.json`. Source witnesses are shared once in `evidence/`; `evidence-index.json` catalogs paths/hashes. All query selections have complete result-to-original mappings, including zero-match errata-register searches. Original corpus objects are reconstructable from verified-equal SQLite raw fields and original field-order metadata, avoiding a redundant second corpus body store.

`helpers/canonical_ro.py` executes the real worktree `tools/gen_alignment_page.py` after checking its exact historical hash. It loads unchanged historical `build_alignment_layer.py` and `hgm_tools.py` bytes, preserves their original module roots, and adapts only SQLite connections to mandatory URI `mode=ro`. It replaces no matching, depth, order, emission or refusal logic. Historical governance/builder objects are actual `git show COMMIT:path` outputs under `native/`, with command/stdin/stdout/stderr/exit retained. External originals are hashed as external bytes, never read through Git.

`native/gen-304-v1.*`, `native/gen-305-v1.*`, `native/gen-306-v1.*` preserve the actual canonical commands, exact input bytes, stdout, stderr and exits. `native/ranges-v1.*` preserves real canonical resolution checks against separately authored intended offsets plus independently parsed HTML ranges, d7 ownership/uniqueness/containment, full original text reconstruction, and historical builder span parsing. All pass. The two sogs → and so on d5 heads have explicit proposed licensors in the mechanical reports; repository allowance registration is a later landing step.

Two helper failures are retained: the report-writing v1 had an unescaped-apostrophe syntax error (exact code and native error saved), fixed without any spec change. The evidence extraction failure is retained: `native/collect-evidence-v1.*` failed on a physical-source byte that is not UTF-8. `helpers/collect_evidence-v1-failed.py` preserves the exact failed script. The successful v2 uses Latin-1 only as a reversible byte-to-codepoint view for ASCII searches, without asserting the publication's encoding. No source text was replaced. The full source bytes are preserved, and whitespace-only line joining proves complete English equality for the three selected physical paragraphs.

No new erratum is filed. In 306 the bracketed author is preserved unwrapped; the exact C15 text, differing ILL verse and nearby ILL context do not by themselves settle attribution or publication independence. No root/other-angle/semantic-stage file was read. A later correction must preserve this freeze and explicitly supersede it.
